---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import registry from '../generated/registry.json';
import coverage from '../generated/coverage.json';
import parameters from '../generated/parameters.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const counts = registry.counts as Record<string, number>;
const unverified = parameters.reduce((n: number, p: { unverified_count: number }) => n + p.unverified_count, 0);
const totalParams = parameters.reduce(
  (n: number, p: { parameters: unknown[] }) => n + p.parameters.length,
  0,
);
const normalized = coverage.totals.normalized;
const expected = coverage.cells.length;
---

<Base
  title="Vermont School Budgets — published, normalized, and modelable"
  description="Every Vermont supervisory union's released budgets in a normalized, documented form, plus a tool to model what merging or closing schools would do to your town's spending and homestead tax rate."
>
  <h1>Vermont school budgets, in the open</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Every Vermont supervisory union's released budgets, published in one normalized form with
    every number traceable to its source — and a tool that lets you model what merging or
    closing schools would do to your town's education spending and homestead tax rate, with
    every step of the arithmetic shown and cited to statute.
  </p>

  <div class="notice blocking">
    <strong>What this site can and cannot tell you today</strong>
    <p>
      The entity registry is complete: {counts['su']} supervisory unions, {counts['ud']} unified
      districts, {counts['school']} schools and {counts['town']} towns, synced from the Agency of
      Education's public data API with every raw response archived.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong style="display:inline">No budget documents have been collected yet</strong> —
      {normalized} of {expected} expected district-years. The
      <a href={`${base}/admin/coverage/`}>coverage dashboard</a> shows exactly which are missing,
      and it is public precisely so the gaps are visible.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong style="display:inline">No statutory parameter has been verified yet</strong> —
      {unverified} of {totalParams}. Until a pupil weight or yield has been read off current
      statute text by a person, the engine refuses to compute with it and returns nothing rather
      than a plausible guess. You will see that refusal, explained, wherever a figure would
      otherwise appear.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Why it is built this way</h2>

  <h3>Provenance is the product</h3>
  <p>
    Every number on this site has to be traceable to a public source. The repository is the
    warehouse: raw budget documents are stored exactly as released, never edited, each with a
    record of where it came from, when, who fetched it, and its SHA-256 hash. When someone asks
    where a number came from and when it changed, the answer is a link to a commit.
  </p>

  <h3>The arithmetic is inspectable</h3>
  <p>
    The modeling engine runs in your browser and its source is open. Its output is not a number
    but a tree: every step carries its inputs, the operation applied, the result, an explanation
    in plain language, and the citation of every statutory parameter used. Independent
    verification is only worth something if the verification can itself be checked.
  </p>

  <h3>Absence is reported, not filled in</h3>
  <p>
    A blank in this site's data means one of two specific things, and it will always say which.
    Either the district did not publish that figure — recorded with who confirmed it and when —
    or a statutory value has not yet been checked against current law. Neither is ever quietly
    replaced with an estimate, and the two are never shown as the same thing.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to start</h2>
  <ul class="grid">
    <li class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0"><a href={`${base}/model/`}>The modeling tool</a></h3>
      <p>Compose a merger or closure scenario and see the arithmetic step by step.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0"><a href={`${base}/su/`}>Supervisory unions</a></h3>
      <p>{counts['su']} profiles: member districts, schools, towns, and budget documents held.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0"><a href={`${base}/methodology/`}>Methodology</a></h3>
      <p>The schema, the engine, every parameter with its citation and verification status.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0"><a href={`${base}/admin/coverage/`}>Coverage</a></h3>
      <p>Which budgets are held, which are missing, and how to send one in.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Neutrality</h2>
  <p>
    This site is independent. It is not produced by, for, or in opposition to the Agency of
    Education, any supervisory union, or any advocacy organization. It computes and explains; it
    does not score, rank, or recommend, and it does not frame any result as a saving. A scenario
    that costs more is presented exactly as prominently as one that costs less, because which of
    those a reader is hoping for is not this site's business.
  </p>
</Base>
